@startuml RAG-Architecture
title Enterprise RAG Architecture — Knowledge Agent

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

component "Knowledge Sources" as Sources {
  [Past FS/TS]
  [Past BRDs]
  [Past Projects]
  [Coding Standards]
  [Architecture Standards]
  [Naming Standards]
  [SAP Standards]
  [Review History]
  [ATC History]
  [Lessons Learned]
}

component "Ingestion & Indexing Worker" as Worker {
  [Connector: SharePoint/OneDrive/Teams\n(Microsoft Graph)]
  [Document Parser\n(PDF/DOCX/HTML/TXT)]
  [Chunker\n(semantic chunking, overlap)]
  [Embedding Generator\n(Azure AI Foundry embeddings)]
  [Dead Link Checker]
  [Lineage Tagger]
}

database "Azure AI Search" as Search {
  [Hybrid Index\n(BM25 + vector fields)]
  [Semantic Ranker]
  [Metadata Filters\n(tenant, sourceType, version, date)]
}

database "PostgreSQL" as PG {
  [knowledge_source]
  [knowledge_chunk]
}

component "Knowledge Agent" as Agent {
  [search_documents()]
  [get_lineage()]
  [check_dead_links()]
}

component "Consumers" as Consumers {
  [FS Agent]
  [TS Agent]
  [RAG Search UI Screen]
}

Sources --> Worker : poll / webhook
Worker --> PG : upsert source + chunk metadata
Worker --> Search : upsert vector + text + metadata fields
Worker --> Worker : detect dead links -> flag is_dead_link
Agent --> Search : hybrid/semantic/vector query + metadata filter
Search --> Agent : ranked results + citations
Agent --> PG : resolve lineage (source -> chunk -> version)
Consumers --> Agent : search_documents(query, filters)

@enduml
